RECORD OF PROCEEDINGS FOR THE GOVERNING BODY
OF THE CITY OF CHEYENNE
Office of City Clerk
October 13, 2008
The Governing Body of the City of Cheyenne met in regular session on this date at 6:00
p.m. in Council Chambers.  Present were: MAYOR-Jack R. Spiker; COUNCIL MEMBERS-Mr.
Brown, Ms. Broyles, Mr. Collins, Mr. Laybourn, Mr. Pierson, Dr. Rinne, Mr. Segrave and Mr.
Valdez.  Absent: Ms. Case.  The pledge of allegiance was recited.

Also present: Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk; Barb Dorr, City Treasurer, and Erik
Rasmussen, Deputy City Attorney.
Mayor Spiker recognized Carol Intlekofer, City Clerk, for recently attaining the
professional designation of Master Municipal Clerk and presented her with a plaque from the
International Institute of Municipal Clerks organization in recognition of the achievement.
Consent Agenda. (All agenda items listed with the designation of [CA] are considered to
be routine items by the governing body and will be enacted by one motion.  There will be no
separate discussion on these items unless a member of the governing body so requests, in which
event the item will be removed from the Consent Agenda and considered in its normal sequence
on the agenda.)  Mr. Collins moved to approve the Consent Agenda items, seconded by Mr.
Segrave.  Motion carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body present with the
exception of Mr. Laybourn voting “no”.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM REGULAR MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
SEPTEMBER 22, 2008.  Motion (per consent agenda) carried.
 [CA]
MINUTES FROM VOUCHERS MEETING OF THE GOVERNING BODY ON
OCTOBER 6, 2008.  Motion (per consent agenda) carried.
Mr. Segrave moved to approve payment of vouchers as presented, seconded by Mr.
Valdez. City Treasurer Barb Dorr requested the following two vouchers be removed for
payment: Cheyenne Chamber of Commerce ($351.00), membership dues for the City’s Taco
John’s Events Center (membership is covered under the City’s general membership dues), and
Wyoming State Bar, ($305.00) annual membership dues for former City Attorney Claudia
Angelos (canceled payment due to Ms. Angelos’ employment resignation).  Mr. Segrave moved
to amend to remove the two vouchers from the payable list as requested by Ms. Dorr, seconded
by Mr. Pierson.  Motion to amend carried.  Voting “yes” – all members of the governing body
present.  Upon inquiry, Ms. Dorr provided information on a voucher payable to John and Wendy
Volk ($5,000.00), earnest money for proposed City acquisition of property for a downtown
parking area (purchase contingent upon approval of the governing body and State Loan and
Investment Board (SLIB) consensus grant funding approval).  Mayor Spiker advised acquisition
of the property would also be contingent upon administrative due diligence.  Comments
followed on the process utilized to negotiate and acquire property; City Council communication;
```

